# Writing requirements

* Produce a book-quality handbook.
* Assume no prior AI knowledge.
* Use the same running observability example throughout the entire book.
* Introduce new concepts only after the prerequisites are understood.
* Frequently refer back to previous chapters so the reader sees how everything connects.
* Prefer visual explanations over long paragraphs whenever possible.
* If a concept can be illustrated with a workflow or diagram, always include one.
* Build from simple to advanced, ending with a complete end-to-end architecture for a production-grade enterprise AI agent.
